{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the son of an Israelite woman went out</b> juxtaposed the blasphemer to the Sabbath gatherer — to teach that the blasphemer and the gatherer were at the same time; and to teach that one who desecrates the Sabbath is like one who denies the fundamental principle." "<b>And they fought</b> Two times: וינצו במחנה and וינצו שניהם בשדה — hint to one who says he went out liable from the court of Moshe because he wanted to pitch his tent in the camp of Dan, and this is וינצו בשדה — on account of a matter of field."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:26.056548597Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}